                <h1>About Clans</h1>
                <p>In the School of Engineering, first-year advising through the Peer Mentoring Program (PMP) is based on a clan system. 
                    Members of each clan consist of a mix of local, mainland and international first-year engineering undergraduates. 
                    Each clan is supported by SENG faculty, staff advisors, and upper-year student mentors. 
                    In addition to providing support and advice through peer advising sessions, your Peer Mentors will organize a variety of 
                    activities in different fields of interest to enhance your first-year experience in the School.</p>
                <p><strong>Your tutorial class number (e.g. T01) in CORE1905B will decide which clan you belong to.</strong></p>
                <p>There will be Clan Orientations on <span style="display:inline-block; color: red">24-26 Aug 2022</span>, please also find the tentative orientation schedule of your clan in the table below:</p>
                <table style="font-family:Segoe, 'Segoe UI', 'DejaVu Sans', 'Trebuchet MS', Verdana, sans-serif;">
                    <tr style="background-color: #d9edf7;">
                      <th>Clan Name</th>
                      <th>CORE1905B Tutorial Class Number</th>
                      <th>Tentative Orientation Date and Time*</th>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <th><span style="color:#000000;">Clan 1 Inno</th>
                      <th>T01-T04</span></th>
                      <th rowspan="3">24 Aug 2022 (Wed), 2:00PM - 4:30PM</th>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <th><span style="color:#46D349;">Clan 2 Eden</span></th>
                      <th><span style="color:#46D349;">T05-T08</span></th>

                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <th><span style="color:#46C2FF;">Clan 3 Galaxy</span></th>
                      <th><span style="color:#46C2FF;">T09-T12</span></th>

                    </tr>
                    <tr>
